<BaseLayout title="How We Create Content" description="How Veldeonix selects topics, researches claims, tests tools, uses AI assistance, reviews, publishes, and corrects content." canonical="/how-we-create-content/">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="narrow"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>How We Create Content</span></div><h1>How we create content</h1><p>A transparent overview of how a Veldeonix tool or guide moves from an idea to a published page.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-tight"><article class="narrow prose"><h2>1. Start with a real task</h2><p>We choose tools around a specific need such as calculating ROI, validating JSON, converting timestamps, or generating a password. We avoid creating pages only to target slight keyword variations.</p><h2>2. Define the method</h2><p>For calculators, we document the formula, units, assumptions, and edge cases. For utilities, we define what data enters the tool, where processing happens, and whether a third-party service is required.</p><h2>3. Research factual claims</h2><p>When a guide depends on a specification, standard, public guideline, or formal definition, we prefer a primary source. Sources are linked when they materially help readers verify a claim.</p><h2>4. Build and test</h2><p>We test normal inputs, empty inputs, invalid values, and common boundary cases. Local-processing disclosures should match the real implementation.</p><h2>5. Draft the explanation</h2><p>Tool pages explain the method, show an example, state limitations, describe privacy behavior, and link to related content only when useful.</p><h2>6. Use AI assistance carefully</h2><p>AI-assisted software can help organize research, produce an outline, review language, or support coding. It does not replace final review. Generated statistics, quotations, citations, company details, and time-sensitive claims should be independently checked.</p><h2>7. Review before publishing</h2><p>We check clarity, tool behavior, internal links, metadata, factual consistency, and privacy disclosures. A high SEO plugin score is not treated as proof of quality.</p><h2>8. Correct and update</h2><p>Confirmed errors are corrected. Material issues can be reported through the <a href="/legal/corrections-policy/">Corrections Policy</a>.</p></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
